I posted one comment, on #1064. The other issues got none, because this session's code commits only touched #1064 and #1012, and #1012 isn't on this list. I didn't close anything.

#1064 (stays open, partly done): I commented on what commit 0d6f8985 did:
• What's fixed: shell hooks now have provider API keys removed from their environment. GITHUB_TOKEN and GH_TOKEN are kept. Hooks start from one place, ShellHook::run_command, so one change covers all three hook phases.
• Default: for hooks the scrub is on unless you turn it off, which is not what the issue planned (it said opt-in). The comment gives the reason: the issue wanted opt-in because the evolve loop runs yoyo -p through the bash tool and needs the key there. Hooks don't do that, and a hook is a script written by the config or the repo. This repo's .yoyo.toml defines no hooks, so the evolve loop is unaffected. YOYO_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=0 or false turns it off, and a blank or misspelled value leaves it on. The model's bash tool is still opt-in, unchanged.
• Tests: the new tests run a real hook. I also broke the default on purpose (made "unset" mean off) and confirmed the right tests failed, then restored it.
• Still open: /run and !, /bg, /watch, sub-agent bash and MCP stdio servers still pass the key to what they start.

The commit is only local so far (8 commits ahead of origin/main); the session wrap-up pushes it, and the comment says so. The deleted session_plan/assessment.md in the working tree was already there, and I left it alone.

